# Builder-3D — project rules (agents)

**Start here:** repository root **`AGENTS.md`** (full playbook). **`DOCS/RULES_AGENTS.md`** — doc workflow detail.

## Must do on every task

1. Read `DOCS/SUMMARY.md` → `DOCS/SCRATCHPAD.md` before coding.
2. Read target files before editing; grep `main.js` — do not assume APIs exist.
3. Match `main.js` / `index.html` / `style.css` patterns; minimal diff scope.
4. **Do not commit or push** unless the user explicitly asks.

## Docs (never delete)

- `DOCS/*`: **append or `[AMENDED date]` only** — never delete/replace existing content.
- During work: update `SCRATCHPAD`; on ship: `CHANGELOG`, `SUMMARY`, and release sync below.

## Release & version

- **`APP_RELEASE`** in `main.js` = canonical semver for modal + `#app-version-pill` + `builder3d-seen-release`.
- Ship checklist: bump **`APP_RELEASE`** + **`package.json` version`** (same string) + top entry **`DOCS/CHANGELOG.md`** + amend **`DOCS/SUMMARY.md`** + **`DOCS/SCRATCHPAD.md`**. See **`DOCS/RULES_RELEASES.md`**.

## Blueprints & saves

- **`BLUEPRINT_VERSION`** (integer schema) ≠ app semver — bump only with backward-compatible import.
- v3: `{ v, site: { outerMaterial, innerMaterial }, parts }` — always use **`buildBlueprintPayload()`** for export/draft/cloud.

## Code constraints

- No new npm deps without **`DOCS/SBOM.md`** + justification.
- New items: `ITEM_TYPES`, `getItemGeometry`, UI `data-item`, help/hints, optional `ARCHITECTURE` note.
- Site ground: `siteGround`, `applyGroundMaterials`; fence: `FENCE_ITEMS` / `trySnapFenceGhost`.
- Shortcuts: `G` grid, `U` grassy yard, `H` paint both grounds, `B` sidebar collapse, `Y` = rotation **axis** (not yard), `C` clone hovered part.
- Sidebar: `#sidebar` full-height dock; `initSidebarChrome` / `initFastTooltips`; `--sidebar-slot-width` for layout + HUD.

## Never

- Force-push main, `git config`, `--no-verify`, or version bump without full release doc sync.
- Hand-build blueprint JSON without `buildBlueprintPayload()`.
